{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1303,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"God, don’t keep silent. Don’t keep silent, and don’t be still, God.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4518},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1304,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"For, behold, your enemies are stirred up. Those who hate you have lifted up their heads.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4522},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1305,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"They conspire with cunning against your people. They plot against your cherished ones.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4525},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1306,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"“Come,” they say, “let’s destroy them as a nation, that the name of Israel may be remembered no more.”","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4528},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1307,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"For they have conspired together with one mind. They form an alliance against you.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4531},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1308,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"The tents of Edom and the Ishmaelites; Moab, and the Hagrites;","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4534},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1309,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"Gebal, Ammon, and Amalek; Philistia with the inhabitants of Tyre;","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4537},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1310,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"Assyria also is joined with them. They have helped the children of Lot. Selah.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4540},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1311,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"Do to them as you did to Midian, as to Sisera, as to Jabin, at the river Kishon;","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4543},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1312,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"who perished at Endor, who became as dung for the earth.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4546},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1313,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"Make their nobles like Oreb and Zeeb, yes, all their princes like Zebah and Zalmunna,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4549},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1314,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"who said, “Let’s take possession of God’s pasture lands.”","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4552},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1315,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"My God, make them like tumbleweed, like chaff before the wind.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4554},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1316,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"As the fire that burns the forest, as the flame that sets the mountains on fire,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4557},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1317,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"so pursue them with your tempest, and terrify them with your storm.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4560},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1318,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"Fill their faces with confusion, that they may seek your name, LORD.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4563},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1319,"verse_start":17,"verse_end":17,"verse_label":"17","text":"Let them be disappointed and dismayed forever. Yes, let them be confounded and perish;","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4566},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:psa","chapter":83,"verse_ordinal":1320,"verse_start":18,"verse_end":18,"verse_label":"18","text":"that they may know that you alone, whose name is the LORD, are the Most High over all the earth.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":4569}]}